    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d20">

                <pb facs="0139" n="13" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg13"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A12/71a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Houghton</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-10-24T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 24,
                                1925—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>322. Probably you have seen press statements on what President said on subject of
                    a disarmament conference. I should be glad if on your own responsibility you
                    could ascertain from the proper British authorities in such a way that it will
                    not be considered an inquiry <pb facs="0140" n="14" xml:id="pg14"/> from this
                    Government what the attitude of that Government is toward the President’s
                    calling of such a conference and what the opinion of British officials is in
                    regard to its reception by other European countries on subjects of both land and
                    naval armament. I am not yet prepared to make inquiry of European countries and
                    for that reason wish this to be simply an informal talk by you on your own
                        responsibility.<anchor n="21" xml:id="d20-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d20-f1" n="21" xml:id="d20-f1-content">
                <p>On Oct. 26, noon, the Ambassador telegraphed that the Department’s inquiry had
                    been fully answered by his telegram No. 332, <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.
                    (File No. 500. A 12/72.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
